                %em Sur les équations différentielles du second ordre et du premier degré dont l’intégrale générale est à points critiques fixes
                Acta Math.
                %strong 33
                (1910) 1–55
          %h4#collection_one_century_later Collection one century later
          %ul
            %li
              %em> The Painlevé property, one century later
              , Robert Conte, ed. CRM Series in Mathematical Physics, Springer, 1999
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-1532-5"} doi
          %p Among the papers in the volume:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Dubrovin"}> Boris Dubrovin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Painlevé transcendents in two-dimensional topological field theory
          %p Another collection
          %ul
            %li
              Théories asymptotiques et équations de Painlevé, Séminaires et Congrès
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 14
          %h4#contemporary_works Contemporary works
          %p Modern viewpoint to R. Fuchs work
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"}> Yuri Manin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Sixth Painlevé equation, universal elliptic curve, and mirror of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi P
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}^2
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9605010"} alg–geom/9605010
          %p
            Connection to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yu.+I.+Manin"}> Yu. I. Manin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rational curves, elliptic curves, and the Painlevé equation
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 321
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511614156.004"} doi
              MR2166923
          %p An arithmetic analogue is studied in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
